Ideally save at least one non-wrest charge for emergency use.
>
> Here is what I am carrying:
>
> +4 Tsurugi of Maramasa (expert)

The tsurugi is a piece of junk, stash it securely (I throw it in a pit
and roll a boulder on it, then write E on the square) unless you don't
have a luckstone.

> +5 Sunsword (expert)

If you're willing to switch back and forth between weapons for big
battles and lack lamps, this can be nice to carry.

> +4 H.Shirt
> +5 GDSM
> +4 Water walking boots/-3 Levitate boots
> +3 Elven Helm
> +3 Cloak of Protection
> +2 GoP (First Wish)
>
> Amulet vs poison

No reflection?  Ugh.  If you can find silver scales somewhere and a
COMR, do that.  If not, if you can find an "oR do that.

Personally I'd ditch the GoP for GoDex or leather and outfit myself
with "oR and a robe.

I'd be on the lookout for jumping boots, too, or at least speed until
you can find jumping.

> Rings of Poly Control and Slow Digest
> also poly/conflict/ invisibility

Conflict, levitation, free action, and telecontrol are the big 4 (the
latter only until you get it intrinsically).

> Lots of wands including 2 poly (4 charges +2recharges), 1 death (8! +
> recharge)
> fire/cold/teleport/dig/sleep

Once you have reflection, keep a fire, death, and teleport in main
inv.  Maybe dig too.

> Lots of scrolls
> 3 identify/3 charging/ 2 gold detect/ 2 genocide (I've already genocided L,h
> and minotaur)

Save one geno and blessed geno ; immediately _after_ entering water.

> and about 12 blank/ 3 mapping

Use the mapping on the Vlad-eligible levels.

> Potions
> 4 full heal/ 3 extra heal/ 2 healing/ 2 speed/ 2 holy water

Save up the healings, speed, and gain energy for alchemy (and as many
